  "method": "Volume calibration updated from Spektor 2011/2016, explained in Text S1 and companion Nisr 2017, doi:10.2138/am-2017-5944; no calibration coefficients in this source supplement. Raman structural OH is qualitative."
 },
 "notes": "Al-free sample; water inferred from volume calibration, not directly measured by SIMS/IR/TGA on this specimen. Raman confirms structural OH qualitatively. Preserve Table 1 Si0.954O2H0.184: its mass-equivalent H2O is about 2.81 wt%, within the reported 3.2(5) wt% range but not exactly its central value. H retention at high pressure is inferred, not measured. No atomic coordinates were refined (Section 2). The 28-42 GPa interval is two-phase coexistence, excluded from both hydrous EOS fits. CaCl2-type Pnnm denotes the Si-O framework refinement model; hydrogen ordering and a possible delta-AlOOH-related subgroup are unresolved (Section 3.2). Table 3 fixed V0=47.191 is retained, not replaced by Table 2 47.198. The cell axes imply 47.198696 A^3. Diffraction uses the explicitly limited peak-position fallback described in source.structure.",
